    "created_at": "2019-07-10T23:12:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-10T23:12:48Z",
    "body": "> Before we go \"in parallel\" we have access to state like this, after we go \"in parallel\" such state is no longer present.\r\n\r\nIs this enforced in the spec? (e.g. if we add `request's element` in the spec, can we reject future PRs that acccess `request's element` after \"in parallel\"?)",
